    "final_text": "The audit is done and the completion receipt is written. The audit turned up one small doc fix; the code change and tests are unchanged.\n\n- **Review:** The `/dxreview` and `/dxverify` skills aren't installed in this session, and no review wrapper was set up. I followed their instructions from the Dex source on disk and ran the review here myself, so no review receipt was published. The first pass found no bugs. It found one gap in the docs: `NaN` used to be dropped and now appears in the URL as `key=NaN`, and the `ISSUE.md` behavior notes didn't say so. I added that in a third commit. A second pass after the fix was clean.\n- **Edge cases I tried:** `NaN`, `-0`, `0n`, empty and nested arrays, objects with no prototype, unicode keys and values, a query that is all `null`, `URLSearchParams` passed straight through, and a query of `0`. All behave correctly, and the caller's query object isn't modified.\n- **Checks:** The syntax check and the targeted tests passed. The full test suite passed on the final tree: 9 of 9, via `dx run-gate --name full-gate`. The project has no formatter, linter, typechecker or build step, so those checks don't apply here.\n- **Branch:** `fix/issue-214-falsy-query-values` has three commits and nothing was pushed, since there's no remote.\n\nPROMPT_COMPLETE",
